WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.010 --> 00:00:03.279
Recently, I posted a story of health insurance on Instagram.

00:00:03.279 --> 00:00:05.839
And my DMs were full of this one question.

00:00:05.839 --> 00:00:08.640
Please suggest the best health insurance for my parents.

00:00:08.640 --> 00:00:13.439
Honestly, this is one of the biggest financial insecurities for all the kids with aging parents.

00:00:13.439 --> 00:00:15.919
Because medical expenses are increasing these days.

00:00:15.919 --> 00:00:23.000
And there are so many wordings and terms and conditions in the insurance policy that you are not sure whether it will be useful or not.

00:00:23.039 --> 00:00:25.760
So, in today's video, we will answer this question.

00:00:25.760 --> 00:00:29.480
How to pick the best health insurance for your parents in 2025?

00:00:29.519 --> 00:00:34.289
In this video, we will see the wordings of the policy, see the data and rank the companies.

00:00:34.320 --> 00:00:35.119
Let's begin.

00:00:37.119 --> 00:00:38.079
First things first.

00:00:38.079 --> 00:00:47.919
Before understanding the details and terms of the policy, we have to see whether all these insurance companies make the life of their consumers easy or difficult when needed.

00:00:53.520 --> 00:00:57.679
So, to understand the credibility of the insurer, we will understand these three metrics.

00:00:57.679 --> 00:01:01.039
The first thing is complaints per 10,000 claims.

00:01:01.039 --> 00:01:05.279
The smoother the claim process of a company, the less complaints will come.

00:01:05.280 --> 00:01:09.519
This is the biggest indicator of how consumer-friendly an insurer is.

00:01:09.519 --> 00:01:12.400
So, here I have the complaints data of all the insurance companies.

00:01:12.400 --> 00:01:14.079
This is the average of the last 3 years.

00:01:14.079 --> 00:01:16.799
To gauge the long-term performance of the company.

00:01:16.799 --> 00:01:22.480
If the complaints volume of any company is more than 20, then that is tricky.

00:01:22.480 --> 00:01:24.879
Anything less than 20 is really good.

00:01:24.879 --> 00:01:31.439
Here, I can see the average complaint volume of Bajaj Allianz in the last 3 years is 3 per 10,000 claims.

00:01:31.439 --> 00:01:32.799
That is really impressive.

00:01:32.799 --> 00:01:38.319
HDFC Ergo has 8, United India has 9, ICICI Lombard has 11.

00:01:38.319 --> 00:01:40.480
So, all these are really good numbers.

00:01:40.480 --> 00:01:47.090
If I talk about the bottom, the worst numbers of Navi are 163 complaints per 10,000 claims.

00:01:47.120 --> 00:01:51.680
After that, Star Health has 46 complaints per 10,000 claims.

00:01:51.680 --> 00:01:53.280
There is a nuance here.

00:01:53.359 --> 00:01:56.079
Navi's complaint number is very high.

00:01:56.079 --> 00:01:59.120
But this doesn't mean that it is worse than Star.

00:01:59.120 --> 00:02:02.480
Navi's total insurance business will be less than 100 crores.

00:02:02.480 --> 00:02:06.560
Star's annual insurance business is more than 10,000 crores.

00:02:06.560 --> 00:02:12.639
So, if the complaint data is so high on that scale, it means that the consumers are not very happy.

00:02:12.639 --> 00:02:15.520
After the complaints data, we will look at the claim settlement ratio.

00:02:15.520 --> 00:02:22.240
CSR tells how much percentage of all the claims in a year is settled by an insurer company.

00:02:22.240 --> 00:02:26.080
The claim settlement ratio should be at least more than 90%.

00:02:26.080 --> 00:02:29.759
If it is less than 90%, then it is still in a risky zone.

00:02:29.759 --> 00:02:32.240
We have the data of the last 3 years.

00:02:32.240 --> 00:02:35.360
HDFC Ergo has the highest claim settlement ratio.

00:02:35.360 --> 00:02:40.159
98%, Digit has 97%, SBI General has 97%.

00:02:40.159 --> 00:02:47.520
If I look at the overall, out of these 24 companies, only 7 companies have less than 90%. The rest are coming in the safe zone.

00:02:47.520 --> 00:02:50.879
In this list, Navi comes in the bottom tier.

00:02:50.960 --> 00:02:52.960
Shriram General comes in the top tier.

00:02:52.960 --> 00:02:56.639
So, the claim settlement ratio of these 2 companies is the worst.

00:02:56.639 --> 00:02:58.240
I would like to give a nuance in this.

00:02:58.240 --> 00:03:02.560
Like other businesses, there are ups and downs in the insurance business too.

00:03:02.560 --> 00:03:11.639
ICICI Lombard whose claim settlement ratio is 88.85% has reduced in recent times due to many reasons.

00:03:11.680 --> 00:03:14.159
Because of which, it is not in the 90% threshold.

00:03:14.159 --> 00:03:25.639
So, if you have ICICI Lombard or any top company's health insurance whose claim settlement ratio is less than 90%, it does not mean that your claim will definitely be rejected.

00:03:25.680 --> 00:03:30.080
You should understand why this claim settlement ratio has reduced.

00:03:30.080 --> 00:03:34.240
The third metric to understand the company's business is the Incurred Claims Ratio.

00:03:34.240 --> 00:03:41.360
ICR tells us how much premium this company has collected in a year versus how much it has returned in claims.

00:03:41.360 --> 00:03:43.360
This is the data of the Incurred Claims Ratio.

00:03:43.360 --> 00:03:52.550
In the last 3 years, if they have collected 100 rupees premiums, instead of that, they have settled a claim of 115 rupees.

00:03:52.560 --> 00:03:54.159
This is not sustainable at all.

00:03:54.159 --> 00:03:58.560
In future, they will have to increase the premiums or they will be able to settle less claims.

00:03:58.560 --> 00:04:04.319
So, the healthy range is 50-90% which are all companies in green.

00:04:04.319 --> 00:04:09.599
This means that companies are able to keep their profits even after settling claims.

00:04:09.599 --> 00:04:10.639
So, it is stable.

00:04:10.639 --> 00:04:18.000
In future, if there are more claims in the next year, then they will be able to settle further claims with these profits.

00:04:18.000 --> 00:04:20.959
So, 50-90% is the ideal range.

00:04:20.959 --> 00:04:33.199
Now, if I add all the 3 metrics and give the final ranking, then in the top tier, HDFC Ergo, Bajaj Alliance, Tata AIG, these 3 companies have performed best in these 3 metrics.

00:04:33.199 --> 00:04:35.199
The bottom results are not surprising.

00:04:35.199 --> 00:04:40.160
Navi is in the last, then Star Health and then Shriram General.

00:04:40.160 --> 00:04:46.160
The concerning thing is that Star Health's total revenue is more than other private insurers.

00:04:46.160 --> 00:04:49.600
Still, their customers are not happy at all.

00:04:49.600 --> 00:04:55.600
So, I hope Star Health improves its experience and service in future.

