00:05:52.160 --> 00:06:00.800
We have learned how to select a company, now let's select a good insurance policy.

00:06:00.800 --> 00:06:04.720
In the world of insurance, remember one thing, the bad cuts out the good.

00:06:04.720 --> 00:06:15.939
Even if your policy has thousands of good benefits, but if your policy has 2-3 red flags, then when you are hospitalized, you will have to take something out of your pocket.

00:06:16.000 --> 00:06:21.279
So, the first thing is, you have to identify the red flags and avoid it in your policy.

00:06:21.360 --> 00:06:28.139
The first red flag is so misunderstood, that people get to know about it only when they get a hospital bill.

00:06:28.160 --> 00:06:29.680
Let me tell you a real-life story.

00:06:29.680 --> 00:06:33.199
In Rajkot, a lady had a medical insurance of 5 lakhs.

00:06:33.199 --> 00:06:39.060
But when she got a bill of 2.5 lakhs, out of that, she had to give 1 lakh to this lady from her pocket.

00:06:39.120 --> 00:06:42.959
Why? Because there was a very big restriction in her policy.

00:06:42.959 --> 00:06:49.360
It was written in her policy that the limit of room rent is up to 1% of the sum assured.

00:06:49.360 --> 00:06:52.959
Meaning, she can't take an expensive room worth more than 5 lakhs.

00:06:52.959 --> 00:06:55.279
The lady didn't like that room worth 5 lakhs.

00:06:55.279 --> 00:07:00.399
She took a room worth 10 lakhs, thinking that whatever extra tariff is there, she will give it from her pocket.

00:07:00.399 --> 00:07:01.759
5 lakhs per day.

00:07:01.759 --> 00:07:03.519
But that's not how it works.

00:07:03.519 --> 00:07:11.040
As your room type or room rent increases, then all your medical costs also increase proportionately.

00:07:11.040 --> 00:07:19.359
Doctor's fees, surgeon charges, OT charges, x-ray, medicines, the fees of all these things can increase.

00:07:19.360 --> 00:07:23.680
And whatever added costs are there, you will have to give it from your pocket.

00:07:23.680 --> 00:07:25.680
This is such a big red flag.

00:07:25.680 --> 00:07:27.199
Look at this policy.

00:07:27.199 --> 00:07:29.439
The sum of 25 lakhs is insured.

00:07:29.439 --> 00:07:32.879
Still, the limit of room rent is up to 10,000.

00:07:32.879 --> 00:07:34.079
How is this fair?

00:07:34.079 --> 00:07:38.000
You took such a big cover that you don't have to give it from your pocket.

00:07:38.000 --> 00:07:43.279
But because of these restrictions, you will have to give a part of the hospital bill from your pocket.

00:07:43.279 --> 00:07:46.800
There is another type of restriction in this, which is room type.

00:07:46.800 --> 00:07:48.079
Look at this policy.

00:07:48.079 --> 00:07:51.360
Covers hospitalization up to the annual sum insured.

00:07:51.360 --> 00:07:54.160
Room rent covered for a single private AC room.

00:07:54.160 --> 00:08:04.040
So, if that lady from Lajkot had this policy, and if she wanted a bigger room than a single private AC room, still, she would have to give a major part of the bill from her pocket.

00:08:04.079 --> 00:08:10.799
So, whenever you are taking a policy, remember the first thing, no room rent or room type restriction.

00:08:10.800 --> 00:08:13.199
Avoid this restriction straight away.

00:08:13.199 --> 00:08:22.370
If you have this restriction in your policy, then either you put an add-on to get rid of this restriction, or you try to port your policy.

00:08:22.399 --> 00:08:31.079
The second red flag, if you have a health insurance of 10 lakhs cover, does it mean that this 10 lakhs will be used in every hospital bill?

00:08:31.120 --> 00:08:32.559
The answer is no.

00:08:32.559 --> 00:08:35.360
And thanks to this bad red flag.

00:08:35.360 --> 00:08:37.519
Look at this insurance policy.

00:08:37.519 --> 00:08:41.360
It is clearly written that robotic surgery is capped at 1 lakh rupees.

00:08:41.440 --> 00:08:48.799
So, even if you have a sum of 10 lakhs insured, still, the reimbursement of robotic surgery will be of 1 lakh only.

00:08:48.799 --> 00:08:51.120
Rest, you will have to give from your pocket.

00:08:51.120 --> 00:09:02.080
There are so many policies in the market, which already mention that even if you have a cover of 10 lakhs, but in all these diseases, you will get only this much from us.

00:09:02.080 --> 00:09:04.399
Rest, you will have to give from your pocket.

00:09:04.399 --> 00:09:08.080
This makes your insurance policy totally useless.

00:09:08.080 --> 00:09:11.519
The name of this red flag is disease-wise sub-limits.

00:09:11.519 --> 00:09:17.919
And whenever you are taking a policy, you have to make sure that there are no such conditions in your policy.

00:09:17.919 --> 00:09:28.399
Now, there is another hidden trap in this, in which many insurance policies not only limit diseases, but also limit particular procedures and medical costs.

00:09:28.399 --> 00:09:29.919
Look at this policy.

00:09:29.919 --> 00:09:37.119
Surgeon, medical practitioner, consultant, specialist fees subject to a maximum of 25% of the sum insured.

00:09:37.120 --> 00:09:48.159
Anesthesia, blood, oxygen, x-ray subject to a maximum of 55% of the sum insured. Remember one thing, the more the sub-limits, the more the complexity.

00:09:48.159 --> 00:09:52.960
The more the complexity, the more difficult it will be to pass the claims.

00:09:52.960 --> 00:09:55.440
This policy is of Star Insurance.

00:09:55.440 --> 00:09:57.330
And after reading these terms and conditions,

00:09:57.360 --> 00:09:59.679
I am not surprised that why people...

00:10:00.000 --> 00:10:02.419
is happy with this insurance company.

00:10:02.419 --> 00:10:05.620
The third red flag is co-payment and deductibles.

00:10:05.620 --> 00:10:16.659
In the case of senior citizens, due to their pre-existing conditions or just due to their age, co-payment or deductibles become mandatory but it is very important to understand its impact.

00:10:16.659 --> 00:10:18.960
Let's understand these two things one by one.

00:10:18.960 --> 00:10:20.500
The first thing is deductibles.

00:10:20.500 --> 00:10:24.700
Suppose in your policy, it is written that some insured 5 lakhs and deductibles 1 lakh.

00:10:24.700 --> 00:10:41.139
This means that if you are hospitalized in the future, then you will pay the first 1 lakh of the hospital bill and after that the extra amount will be paid by the health insurance company. Suppose your bill is 3 lakhs, then you will pay the first 1 lakh

00:10:41.139 --> 00:10:45.779
and the remaining 2 lakhs will be paid by the insurance company.

00:10:45.779 --> 00:10:53.000
If your hospital bill is 40,000 rupees, then you will have to pay the entire 40,000 rupees in that case.

00:10:53.000 --> 00:10:55.000
There are two types of deductibles.

00:10:55.000 --> 00:11:00.000
One is the absolute deductible, which means that 1 lakh is paid once in a year.

00:11:00.000 --> 00:11:06.639
And the second is the per-claim deductible, which means that whenever you claim, then you have to pay 1 lakh yourself.

00:11:06.659 --> 00:11:13.240
So, if deductibles are compulsory for your parents, then make sure that it is a once-a-year deductible.

00:11:13.240 --> 00:11:17.500
That you have to pay a total of 1 lakh at a time and not every time.

00:11:17.500 --> 00:11:20.500
The second cost-sharing method is co-payment.

00:11:20.500 --> 00:11:30.470
This means that every time there is a hospital bill, the policyholder has to pay a certain percentage of the bill and the rest will be covered by the health insurance company.

00:11:30.500 --> 00:11:42.239
For example, if there is a 20% mandatory co-payment in your policy and the hospital bill is 3 lakhs, then you will have to pay 60,000 rupees from your pocket and the remaining amount will be paid by the health insurance company.

00:11:42.240 --> 00:11:47.240
Again, like deductibles, many times co-payment is also mandatory for senior citizens.

00:11:47.240 --> 00:11:52.240
But you should try to find a policy where there is no co-payment.

00:11:52.240 --> 00:12:02.200
If we compare deductible and co-pay, then suppose you have a small deductible of 50,000 rupees and you have a bill of 5 lakhs, then you will have to pay 50,000 rupees.

00:12:02.240 --> 00:12:05.240
If you have a bill of 10 lakhs, then you will have to pay 50,000 rupees.

00:12:05.240 --> 00:12:13.240
But in the case of co-payment, as the hospital bill increases, your expense will also increase.

00:12:13.240 --> 00:12:18.240
So in general, a small amount of deductible is way better than opting for co-payment.

00:12:18.240 --> 00:12:21.240
But ideally, both should not be there.

00:12:21.240 --> 00:12:26.240
We have discussed the red flags, now let's talk about the good things to have in your parents' insurance policy.

00:12:26.240 --> 00:12:39.240
First things first, as our age increases, pre-existing conditions like diabetes, hypertension, asthma come.

00:12:39.240 --> 00:12:43.240
And the waiting period for these pre-existing conditions is very long.

00:12:43.240 --> 00:12:48.240
Many times, the insurance policy will say that these conditions will not be covered for 3-4 years.

00:12:48.240 --> 00:13:00.240
So in this case, if you are taking an insurance policy and if your diabetic father has to be hospitalized for some diabetic issue, then that will not be covered for the first 4 years. This is very very bad.

00:13:00.240 --> 00:13:04.240
So the smart thing to do is to look for a policy with a shorter waiting period.

00:13:04.240 --> 00:13:10.240
Or the second option is to buy an add-on which will reduce the waiting period.

00:13:10.240 --> 00:13:12.240
Look at this policy.

00:13:12.240 --> 00:13:15.240
In this policy, there was a waiting period of 3 years for diabetes.

00:13:15.240 --> 00:13:20.240
But by taking this instant cover add-on, you will get this cover from day 1.

00:13:20.240 --> 00:13:24.240
Of course, the 30-day waiting period is for everyone.

00:13:24.240 --> 00:13:30.240
So if you are buying a policy, no hospitalization expenses are covered in the first 30 days.

00:13:30.240 --> 00:13:39.240
After that, such an add-on covers all your pre-existing conditions after the 30th day itself.

00:13:39.240 --> 00:13:44.240
Second must have, always make sure that your parents' cover is very high.

00:13:44.240 --> 00:13:51.240
Many children take a family floater insurance plan for their wife and parents.

00:13:51.240 --> 00:13:53.240
There are two risks in this.

00:13:53.240 --> 00:14:04.220
First risk, if you or your wife get hospitalized for any reason, then in the future, your parents who have a higher risk of getting hospitalized, will have less cover for them.

00:14:04.240 --> 00:14:13.179
Second thing, if your parents get hospitalized and the cover is exhausted, then the whole family will not have health insurance for a long time.

00:14:13.240 --> 00:14:16.240
So please don't think of saving premiums.

00:14:16.240 --> 00:14:19.240
Take a separate health insurance for your parents.

00:14:19.240 --> 00:14:23.240
The ideal setup should be that you buy a health insurance worth Rs. 10 lakhs.

00:14:23.240 --> 00:14:26.240
If you want to buy more than that, then you can buy it.

00:14:26.240 --> 00:14:33.239
But if the premiums are unaffordable, then you should take a policy which has an automatic restoration benefit.

00:14:33.240 --> 00:14:42.239
This means that if the cover is exhausted after the hospital bill, then this policy will automatically fill your cover again.

00:14:42.240 --> 00:14:44.240
Look at the wording of this policy.

00:14:44.240 --> 00:14:56.230
The company shall instantly add 100% of the base sum insured under this benefit in the event of an admissible claim during the policy year due to which sum insured was partially or completely exhausted.

00:14:56.240 --> 00:15:02.389
This means that even if you are using partially, still this insurance company will add Rs.

00:15:02.389 --> 00:15:04.190
2 lakhs for you.

00:15:04.240 --> 00:15:11.200
In many insurance policies, it also happens that until the entire sum insured is not exhausted, they will not restore.

00:15:11.240 --> 00:15:16.240
Ideally, pick one which restores the cover even if it is partially used.

00:15:16.240 --> 00:15:21.239
If these restoration benefit policies are not available, then the second option is to buy a super top-up.

00:15:21.240 --> 00:15:24.240
Buy a sum insured worth Rs. 10 lakhs.

00:15:24.240 --> 00:15:28.240
After that, buy a super top-up plan worth Rs. 20-30 lakhs.

00:15:28.240 --> 00:15:35.239
As soon as your sum insured is exhausted, this super top-up plan will be activated.

00:15:35.240 --> 00:15:42.239
And then the rest of the medical bill, the hospital bill, will be monitored by this super top-up plan.

00:15:42.240 --> 00:15:45.240
You have to buy this super top-up insurance separately.

00:15:45.240 --> 00:15:47.240
And it is very affordable.

00:15:47.240 --> 00:15:58.200
If your parents are eligible for super top-up, then this is a great feature to have to increase your cover without paying an exorbitant amount in every year premiums.

00:15:58.240 --> 00:16:01.240
The third green flag is very overlooked.

00:16:01.240 --> 00:16:04.240
But in the case of senior citizens, it becomes mandatory.

00:16:04.240 --> 00:16:06.240
It is home care treatment.

00:16:06.240 --> 00:16:11.240
The reality is that being hospitalized every time along with the age is not feasible.

00:16:11.240 --> 00:16:17.239
So many times doctors will also recommend to keep a round of chemotherapy or dialysis at home.

00:16:17.240 --> 00:16:25.210
And in such cases, if there is no day care treatment in your insurance policy, then you will have to pay this bill from your pocket.

00:16:25.240 --> 00:16:31.240
Or you will have to be hospitalized mandatorily for every treatment.

00:16:31.240 --> 00:16:34.240
And that is an added burden when your parents are aging.

00:16:34.240 --> 00:16:35.240
See this policy.

00:16:35.240 --> 00:16:38.240
It is clearly written in this policy that we pay for chemotherapy taken at home.

00:16:38.240 --> 00:16:40.240
We pay for dialysis taken at home.

00:16:40.240 --> 00:16:50.179
And if the doctor is advising that the person should undergo treatment at home, then in that case also, the expense is borne by the insurance company.

00:16:50.240 --> 00:16:56.239
In parents' insurance, domiciliary treatment and home care expenses should definitely be covered.

00:16:56.240 --> 00:16:59.240
The fourth and last green flag is very personal.

00:16:59.240 --> 00:17:00.240
But I swear by it.

00:17:00.240 --> 00:17:08.240
After the age of 25, I feel that every person should get a full body checkup every 6 months or a year.

00:17:08.240 --> 00:17:11.210
When I got my full body checkup done 2 years ago,

00:17:11.240 --> 00:17:14.240
I realized that I have a non-alcoholic fatty liver.

00:17:14.240 --> 00:17:17.240
And this is a disease that has no symptoms.

00:17:17.240 --> 00:17:23.239
So if I had got this full body checkup done after 5 years, then the situation would have gotten even worse.

00:17:23.240 --> 00:17:26.240
And in that case, I would have had to undergo major treatments.

00:17:26.240 --> 00:17:29.240
After that one health checkup, my fitness journey started.

00:17:29.240 --> 00:17:32.240
Thankfully, my fatty liver is over today.

00:17:32.240 --> 00:17:36.240
And most of the lifestyle diseases are like this.

00:17:36.240 --> 00:17:38.240
Symptomless for the first 5-10 years.

00:17:38.240 --> 00:17:43.239
And when you start seeing symptoms, then it becomes very severe.

00:17:43.240 --> 00:17:47.240
For which you will have to start a treatment or it is irreversible.

00:17:47.240 --> 00:17:50.240
So please get a health checkup done regularly.

00:17:50.240 --> 00:17:54.240
In the case of parents, it should be mandatory every 6 months.

00:17:54.240 --> 00:17:57.240
My parents also get their full body checkup done regularly.

00:17:57.240 --> 00:18:02.220
Now there are many such insurance policies, in which you get a free annual health checkup.

